<Base title="About | Fate Apothecary" description="About Fate Apothecary — a living cookbook of food, herbs, and kitchen intuition.">
  <article class="about-page shell">
    <header class="about-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Fate Apothecary</p>
      <h1>Food, herbs, and a little kitchen intuition.</h1>
      <p class="about-lede">Fate Apothecary started with herbs and the idea that the things we keep in our kitchens can be useful, nourishing, comforting, and worth understanding.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>Over time, I realized the kitchen was always the bigger story.</p>
      <p>I love to cook, but I am not a precise cook. I rarely measure unless it actually matters. I taste, adjust, substitute, use what I have, and frequently claim that my ancestors tell me when to stop adding ingredients.</p>
      <p>This is a living cookbook for the food I really make: gluten-free, almost entirely dairy-free, nitrate-conscious, practical family food, freezer staples, pantry basics, herbs, and whatever else earns a permanent place in my kitchen.</p>
      <p>The goal is not to make your food taste exactly like mine. It is to give you enough information to make something delicious in <em>your</em> kitchen — and eventually trust yourself enough to cook with your heart.</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="about-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">One important note</p>
      <p>Fate Apothecary shares food, cooking, and traditional herbal knowledge for general informational purposes. Nothing here is a substitute for individualized medical advice.</p>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Base>
